@carole.hooven ❤️ I would genuinely love to learn more about this from you. It would be wonderful if you ever considered starting your own podcast on hormonal diversity across biological sexes—especially focusing on androgen biology.

In particular, I would be very interested in a deep dive on androgen receptors: the most current and fine-tuned research on how we define, detect, differentiate, and evaluate androgen receptor density. Beyond density alone, it would be fascinating to explore all the other dimensions that determine how effectively an organism can utilize androgens—such as receptor sensitivity, co-regulators, tissue-specific expression, epigenetic regulation, intracellular signaling pathways, and other emerging mechanisms that may not yet be fully understood.

A thoughtful overview of the current scientific landscape—and the methodological challenges in measuring and interpreting androgen receptor activity—would be incredibly valuable for those interested in endocrinology, physiology, and human variation.

